                <pb facs="0090" n="60" xml:id="pg60"/>

                <head>31. Editorial Note</head>
                <p>The 13th regular session of the U.N. General
                    Assembly opened at 3 p.m., Tuesday, September 16. Sir Leslie Munro, President of the 12th General
                    Assembly, presided over the opening, appointment of a Credentials Committee, and
                    election of a President. Prior to the election, Czechoslovakia withdrew the
                    candidacy of Jiři Nosek in favor of
                        Mohammed Ahmed Mahgoub of Sudan. The
                    General Assembly then elected Charles Malik of Lebanon President of the 13th session, casting 45 votes
                    for Malik, 31 for Mahgoub, and 4 abstentions. Malik assumed the Chair immediately after the
                    elections. For a record of these proceedings, see U.N. doc. APV.747.</p>
            </div>
